course: dictionary
lesson: 14341
title: Oceanic and the ocean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Oceanic is an adjective, so it describes a noun. Its main meaning is to do with the ocean, or living in it. The clue is inside the word: «ocean» plus «-ic», which means "to do with". «The albatross is an oceanic bird, and it can spend months far out over the sea.»
explain: Context can also show a second meaning, like an ocean: very big and wide. «The field was oceanic, so wide and flat that we could not see the far edge.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Try "to do with the ocean" first. It does not make sense, so look for "very big and wide" instead.
explain: In geography, oceanic can mean to do with Oceania, the region of Australia, New Zealand and the Pacific islands. «Our project is about the oceanic islands.» Use the topic to decide which meaning fits. A geography lesson often means the region, not the sea.
fact: Oceanic is an adjective, so you can say an oceanic climate or an oceanic animal.
fact: «Oceanic» means to do with the ocean, or living in the ocean.
fact: «Oceanic» can also mean like an ocean: very big and wide.
fact: In geography, «oceanic» can mean to do with Oceania, the region of Australia, New Zealand and the Pacific islands.
fact: Phrases to know: «oceanic crust» is the rock under the oceans, «oceanic trench» is a very deep crack in the ocean floor, and an «oceanic climate» is mild and wet.
exercise: «Whales and albatrosses are oceanic animals.» What does oceanic mean here? | *Living in or to do with the ocean | Sleepy and slow | Made of sand | Very tall and thin
exercise: «The explorers crossed the oceanic plain, and the grass seemed to have no end.» What does oceanic suggest? | Hot and dusty | *Very big and wide, like an ocean | Dry and sandy | Small and shallow
exercise: «We learned about the oceanic islands of Oceania.» Which region is Oceania? | The Arctic ice cap | The Sahara desert | *Australia, New Zealand and the Pacific islands | The mountains of Europe
test:
«The oceanic trench was the deepest part of the sea.» What is an oceanic trench? | *A very deep crack in the ocean floor | A high mountain ridge on land | A small pond with still water | A type of ship
Mild and wet is what an oceanic climate is like, as in Ireland and New Zealand. What is an oceanic climate? | Very hot and dry all year | *Mild and wet, like Ireland and New Zealand | Freezing cold with deep snow | Windy with no rain at all
exam: Ruby says oceanic only means fish. What is the best reply? | *No, it means to do with the ocean, and it can also mean very big and wide | Yes, it only means things on land | No, it means very hot and dry | Yes, it only ever means fish
